From ccf28bc655105e8da95d99c0b9d80db68ee94399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:45:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] WIP HC16: native-BF16 producers for the HC gate and
 normalized stream

Session 8 of the bf16-producer port (wip/mmb-general/BF16-PRODUCER-PORT.md).

- mark lifetime: clear the BF16-only marks on the first optimize after a compute
  (the scheduler optimizes every split before computing any of them, so the
  marks must survive the remaining splits' optimize calls), and add the marking
  pass: a gated DSV4_HC_PRE whose gate (dense MUL_MAT [320 x 10240]) is MMB-taken
  and whose only consumer is that op marks the gate output BF16-only.
- MMB dense now allocates its pinned slot 1 for that gate from the mark alone
  (it no longer requires mmb_hc16()); dsv4_hc_pre reads the BF16 copy through a
  new `wbf16` arm.  The gate round trip is bf16(4B write) instead of
  f32 write + f32 read = a real numerics change.
- the fused rms_norm+mul of the HC normalized stream (broadcast [n_embd, hc]
  gamma over a 3D [n_embd, hc, nt] activation) also emits a BF16 copy into slot
  0, rounded exactly as mmb_cvt_f32_bf16, so the following MMB dense down
  projection skips its own conversion pass.  That copy is bit-identical, so the
  GEMM result is unchanged.

Measured gfx1151, IQ4_XS Flash-Next, bf16 KV, -b/-ub 2048, MMB+QSA3 on:
pp8192 950.8 -> 961.9 t/s (+1.2%), pp2048 973.1 -> 994.2 (+2.2%); the xn copy
is bit-identical (PPL c2048 10.6428 both with and without it) and the same-seed
greedy text is unchanged.  The gate BF16 is the only numerics change
(PPL c2048 10.5771 -> 10.6428, within the run's +-0.68 bar).  All behind
GGML_CUDA_MMB_HC16=1.
